      "Formula.leanConditions walks the formula and returns, without duplicates, the condition of each implies whose consequent is not ff (implies a ff is not a) and the second argument of each precedes, descending through and, or, words and the primitive operators, and not into not, never, stronglyImplies' and leadsTo's conditions, outcomes, follows, transition or final. Logic.checkCtl, the one place session_ctl, check_ctl and requirement entries are decided, takes those conditions when the formula holds and evaluates (ef c) for each over the same model (Model.satE, same bounds); the ones false at the start make the verdict vacuous, the reading is prefixed proved only because ... never happens:, and vacuousParts lists each with notation and reading. RequirementCtl counts only proved as met, so vacuous fails. Formula.ifEver a b is read from {\"ifEver\": [a, b]} and (ifEver a b), means implies everywhere (expand, negate, the tree and DAG evaluators, unfold), reads as if (a) ever happens, then (b), and is written ifEver(a, b); leanConditions does not descend into its condition, and Formula.neverConditions collects those conditions so checkCtl reports the unreachable ones as neverHappens with a note in the reading, leaving the verdict proved."
