      "LeanFM.Signal: Claim is above, below, on, not, and, or, implies, within, throughout, always, never, possibly and inevitably, read from an s-expression by its own reader of names, numbers and parentheses (no labels, nothing evaluated), at most 256 words. Samples come from samples (t, label, numeric fields) or from log (event lines: ts / 1e9 seconds, label, payload numbers), sorted check refusing the first out of order, at most 100000. start is the first index at which every field the claim reads has had a reading (a field never read is refused); Claim.leaves lists the leaves (above, below, on); a leaf starts at its field's first-reading index, or 0 for on, and a node at the latest start of its leaves, so the nodes' starts differ exactly when the leaves' do; without from, a claim whose leaves' starts differ is refused before margin runs, naming a leaf with the latest start and one with the earliest; with from, start is the first index whose t is at least from, and a field whose first reading comes after start is refused. The samples before start are dropped and counted as skipped, and hold fills each field forward over the whole run, keeping the values from start on, so a field read before start carries its latest earlier reading in. margin computes one Float array per claim node, bottom up: above and below subtract, on is +inf or -inf, not negates, and and or take min and max pointwise, implies is max of the negated condition and the result, always and never take a suffix minimum, possibly and inevitably a suffix maximum, and within and throughout a sliding maximum and minimum over [t, t+d] with a monotone deque (each index pushed and popped once), counting the moments whose window reaches past the last sample. margin's state is a Tally of cut-short moments and steps: a leaf, not and implies add n, and and or add n per part, always, never and possibly add n, and slide adds one per loop pass, deque push, pop and head advance (at most 4n); check sums the steps of both margin passes and refuses, as an internal error, steps over stepBound = 10 × Claim.size × n, answering steps and stepBound otherwise. The verdict is the margin at the first sample; for an always or never the first sample whose inner margin is negative is reported with its readings. num writes a finite margin rounded to 3 decimals and an infinite one as the string unbounded or -unbounded. plot draws the chart for theme light or dark: per field a 460 by 150 panel scaled to the readings and bounds, a polyline of at most 2000 points, a dashed line per bound (Claim.bounds), red circles at the samples whose inner margin is negative (at most 400, the rest counted in the panel's caption), a tick per sample whose label the claim names (Claim.labels), day marks when the run spans a day; every name passes through esc. Logic.run dispatches check_signal, measuring the 64 KiB argument bound without the log when logWindow is present (the server read it); MCP.lean lists it with its schema and, for check_signal as for session_conform, replaces serverLog with the window ServerLogs.logArgs reads (logWindow beside it; LeanFMMcp models Disk reads for session tools only, so this one is not traced); ServerLogs.sources gains devices (logs/devices.log). check answers source {kind log, log, fromLine, lastLine, logLines} when logWindow is present, else {kind given, samples}."
