      "LeanFM.Session.Text reads protocol text with the grammar of LeanFM.Session.Grammar (decision session-lean-syntax): Lean's parser and token rules over the text, never elaboration, then a conversion of the syntax tree into Stmt values with every limit checked (statements, branches, depth, names and strings, numbers, durations and samples), errors carrying line and column; it builds Global String with the protocol command's semantics (choice and rec continue with Global.andThen, include renames the earlier protocol's roles and becomes a box), counting statements. Text.write prints statements back as text, and SessionTools.ToText writes a JSON protocol as text (includes become earlier protocols over the same roles). parseProtocol takes lean first; otherwise it reads {name?, roles, steps} with a StateT step counter over Except: each step must have exactly one kind key and only that kind's keys; strings are non-empty, at most 200 characters and free of control characters; roles are distinct and at most 12; a msg becomes an Interaction (its where text a Guard), event becomes act, choice and rec continue with Global.andThen, parallel, join, sessions and include (box) carry their continuation, continue must name an enclosing rec and end its branch; errors name the step path such as steps[1].choice[0].steps[2]. check runs Global.issues, Global.project with Local.render and Local.typestate per role, Global.calls and callsText, Global.diagramModel (as shape JSON) and, with mayCall, Global.httpCuts with every channel HTTP. diagram adds DiagramModel.svg in the requested theme. simulate wraps a protocol without a sessions block in sessions and runs Global.simulate with bounded seed, instances, spread, loops and maxEvents. fit keeps the compressed answer under 90,000 characters by setting svg and then diagram to null and halving the events, listing what it left out. conform reads events with logEvent (string or number ids, sessions and causes; from/to or src/dst; at with act for an event; at most 2000 events), runs Global.conforms and lists each failing session's first problem as issues; compat parses the new version from lean and the old from old (an error names which), runs Global.compat on the bodies of their top-level sessions blocks with each version's roles, and answers a row per shared role with ok, reason and the path (after), the issues with their paths, the upgrade order, and notes naming roles in one version only; next reads the walk's events with logEvent (at most limits.maxSteps), runs Global.next and answers each NextStep as {label, from, to | act, cause?} with canEnd; skeleton runs Global.pythonSkeleton (language python only) and MCP.logicResult appends a result's code to its text content; the prompt design_with_session_types is MCP.sessionDesignPrompt. MCP.toolResult tries SessionTools.run before the logic tools and wraps the answer with logicResult (one-line summary, structuredContent); the reference is the resource leanfm://language/session-reference, and the server instructions point to it."
      ["LeanFM/SessionToolsTests.lean: the text parser agrees with the protocol command (diagram, issues and every projection) on Purchase, Transfer, TransferWithTimer, ReplicatedOrder with include and join, PurchaseHttp and Serve; the reference's Lean example checks ok and draws the same diagram and calls as its JSON example; a JSON protocol's echoed text reads back to the same diagram; unknown roles, missing ';', unclosed braces, comments and strings, continue outside rec or not last, missing or misused include, repeated roles and joins out of range are rejected with line and column; a #eval line and a where condition with Lean code are syntax errors, never run; PlaceOrder in JSON checks ok with the client's typestate and calls; the race, the bank that cannot tell and a borrowed cause are reported as in SessionTests; mayCall reports Paid going to the shop; unknown roles, keys and kinds, continue outside rec or not last, join out of range, too many roles or steps, deep nesting and control characters are rejected with the path; a where text is never evaluated; the same arguments give the same answer; a large simulation stays under 90,000 characters and says what it left out", "LeanFM/MCPTests.lean: tools/list has the three tools; tools/call session_check answers through the MCP dispatch with a one-line summary", "LeanFM/SessionToolsTests.lean: the worked example examples/vibecode/lending: its protocol checks clean, its README picture is the generated dark diagram (a C2PA provenance metadata element, which file delivery may add, set aside; any change to what is drawn fails), the log written by lending.py conforms (80 events in 20 sessions) and the log of its --bug Desk is reported at sessions 5 and 12 with Lent where the protocol allows Waitlisted"]
