900, then -jpeg -jpegopt quality=70 at 900, 60 at 760, 55 at 640 and 45 at 520, each with ProjectView.runBounded (IO.Process.spawn with no shell and the arguments as an array, stdout drained in a task, tryWait polled until renderTimeoutMs, 10000, then kill and an error naming the page and the limit), keeping the first image of at most maxImageBytes (48000) and returning it as base64 with its MIME type; a page no rung fits is refused naming the bound. Nothing is written: the cache is memory only and the oldest entry is dropped beyond 64. ProjectView.pageOf turns an array of items into one page from an offset: items in order while there are at most pageItems (100) and their JSON is at most pageChars (40000) characters (always at least one), each item first through fitItem, which cuts every string in an item longer than itemChars (8000) characters to that length and marks it cut; the page carries offset, total, next (null on the last page) and items. requirements without section answers sections [{name, count}] for tasks, clauses and protocols; section tasks pages task summaries (id, title, actors, states and the counts of transitions, properties and constraints); section transitions, properties or constraints with task pages that task's list (an unknown task is refused naming the section); section clauses pages SelfHosting.clauses; section protocols pages the protocol files. For LeanFM the task JSON is built in Lean from SelfHosting.spec (tasks, transitions with their actors, properties with propertyFormula, requiredProofs as AG not, where_ constraints from ChatUI taskConstraints minus SharedProjects.replacedConstraints plus SharedProjects.constraints, as the old /tasks route did) and SelfHosting.clauses; for another project it parses spec/tasks.json (read at most 4 MiB) and passes its tasks through. protocols lists .leanfm and .protocol files under the root, skipping .git, .lake, .cache, node_modules and (for LeanFM) projects/, at most 2000; file returns one of them as lean, refused when it is over textPageChars (40000) characters since session_explore needs it whole. code lists source files (LeanFM: the root's files with source extensions under the same skips; others: the manifest's source directory) a page at a time with pageOf, each with the indices of the traceability mappings that name it, and the mappings by name and requirements only (LeanFM: McpLogicImplementation.decisions and SessionImplementation.decisions as requirements = refs, files, tests; others: source/traceability.json mappings); file returns, without the listing, the file's text (at most 256 KiB read, UTF-8) from a character offset for at most textPageChars characters with total and next, and the full mappings that name it, and a file not in the listing is refused. ProjectView.answer measures every answer it builds: when the text and the compressed structured content together are over maxAnswerChars (70000) it returns an error naming the bound and the narrower question to ask instead of the answer. ProjectView.enabled is ServerLogs.enabled itself, the one switch McpServer.lean (--stdio, or LEANFM_MCP_LOGS=1) and Server.lean turn on, so project_view and server_logs are served in exactly the same places; MCP.listedTools adds the tool only then and tools/call refuses it otherwise. SessionView.html draws the navigator bar first in the view (chat, book, requirements, code and a select of project names), calls project_view through the same single in-flight queue as its other tools, draws the chat log as text with an Older messages button while older is set, the page as an img with a data: URL built only from the base64 field and one of the fixed types image/png and image/jpeg, the requirements overview as one button per section with its count, a section's page as text rows (a task's row opens its transitions, properties and constraints) with a Next page button while next is set, protocols as rows that load the file and call session_explore with its text, the source