      ["LeanFM/MCPTests.lean: project_view lists Maqam's implementations (rust, zig) and its default in every answer; the spec overview names spec/Requirements.lean, spec/Requirements.proto and spec/Maqam.leanfm, Requirements.lean opens as text, a source file is refused there; the overview's primary is spec/Maqam.leanfm for Maqam, LeanFM/LLMGenerated/LeanFM.leanfm for LeanFM and spec/PaxosKV.leanfm for PaxosKV, and primaryProtocol of a project with no protocol files is none; Maqam's written book is found, and a project root with neither a PDF nor book/main.tex answers found false and written false and says it has not been written, never to run make book; impl shows impl/zig/Implementation.lean (the default) and impl/rust/Implementation.lean with impl rust, each with its check and every error it listed; code for Maqam shows impl/zig/source by default with its mapping and check, and only impl/rust/source with impl rust; another implementation's file, an unlisted impl and impl for GoServer (no implementations) are refused; scripts/session_view_smoke.js: the bar is the pickers row then book, spec, impl, code; spec lands in session_explore on LeanFM/LLMGenerated/LeanFM.leanfm (the overview's primary) with its tree shown and the spec row marking the explorer, and files & sections lists SelfHosting.lean and the protocols and opens the text in one click; impl shows the mapping; picking Maqam shows an implementation picker defaulting to zig with its check, and picking rust asks project_view for code with impl rust; project_view lists LeanFM first and the projects with a manifest; a project given as a path or with .. is refused; chat for LeanFM says where the conversation happens; ProjectView.chatMessages decodes saved log lines, checked on a fixture line (its text base64, an sk- key in it redacted, a malformed line dropped), so the test needs no conversation on disk; and chat for GoServer decodes its saved log when the checkout has one and otherwise says where the conversation lives (conversations are never committed, so a fresh checkout, such as CI's, has none); book returns a page image of at most 48000 bytes and the page count, the same page again from the cache without a render, and a render that outlives its limit is killed and refused; every stage of LeanFM and of GoServer answers under 70000 characters, and an answer built over the bound is refused naming it; requirements for LeanFM without section lists tasks, clauses and protocols with their counts, its tasks page carries selfhost_workflow, the workflow's properties page its CTL formulas (AF) and a never proof, its constraints page where_ constraints, the clauses pages reach the navigator clause through next, and an item over 8000 characters is cut and marked; a missing or unknown task is refused; code for LeanFM lists LeanFM/ProjectView.lean with a mapping naming clause:selfhost.mcp.session.navigator; a file outside the listing, an absolute path and a symlink out of the root are refused; the tool is unlisted and refused while disabled; the view's navigator draws the four stages and the chat stage has no input, textarea or form (driven in Node against the stub DOM)"]
