      ["panel(title, child) folds when the text under it runs over FOLD_LINES (15) lines: it returns foldPanel(title + ', N lines', child, false); the roles' typestates are one panel each in a single column (.roles is a block, not a grid), each foldPanel closed; pre in a panel wraps (white-space: pre-wrap). LeanFM/SessionView.lean", "LeanFM/SessionView.html", "LeanFM/MCP.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Diagram.lean"]
      "SessionView.sessionViewUri is ui://leanfm/session-view/ followed by the hex of hash sessionViewHtml, so the URI changes exactly when the view does; MCP.resourceRead answers it and the bare ui://leanfm/session-view with the same document. streamView's onFocus also tells the answer's sequence diagram panel which labels the focused thread has (focusLabels, a set the diagram panel listens to); diagram(model, {labels}) treats an item whose message label is in the set as selected, so openAround opens its folds and frames and the drawing lights it, and a note above the drawing names the thread; Show all events sends the empty set. Threads in colour: every stream event carries thread, the actor that sent it: LogSessions.stream writes the event's Role/instance, or Role@session (its log session, or its derived one) when the log names only the role, as Actors.src does; SessionTools.eventJson writes Role@session for a simulated event. SessionView.html defines --t0 to --t7 for both themes and classes thr0 to thr7 that set --thr; streamView numbers threads in order of first appearance modulo 8, draws a Threads legend (each name in its colour, at most MAX_ITEMS listed and the rest counted) and passes animation opts.threadOf, so tint draws an event in its thread's colour (bad statuses stay --bad; a stream without thread keeps the kind colours) and each log row gets thr and thrN; a session filter passes the same threadOf, so colours do not change. Lifelines per actor: LogSessions.stream writes srcActor and dstActor (the logged Role/instance, or the role); animation's laneOf reads them, falling back to src and dst, and lanes lists, for each role in body.roles, its actors in order of first appearance (the role itself when no event names one), then any other actor; columns, arrows, prior links, cause curves, frames, the header and the log rows use lanes, and a role focus still marks the events whose role is the focus. Highlight: streamView adds a select (aria-label Highlight one