SON; drawPropForm and the pattern builder write the formula with JSON.stringify(f, null, 2). In the animation, links (prior, cause, answers) are resolved through a map from event id to position, and sessionBody keeps ids and drops links to events it leaves out; causeLanes gives every event with a cause an interval from its cause's row to its own and puts it in the first lane whose last interval ended before it starts (outer intervals first), and the canvas reserves a gutter of ten pixels per lane right of the last lifeline for the brackets; threadOf follows prior links back (ancestors) and forward (the events naming it in prior) from an event; a click on an event's row in the canvas calls streamView's onFocus with the thread's ids, which rebuilds the animation over sessionBody of exactly those events, paused at its end with the event selected, roles with no event left named as hidden and a Show all events button; animSessions, set by a number input clamped to 1..MAX_ANIM_SESSIONS (200, limits.maxInstances), is sent as instances with maxEvents MAX_EVENTS (600) by Animate and by the animate view. SessionView.html speaks the MCP Apps handshake (ui/initialize, ui/notifications/initialized, tool-result, host-context-changed, size-changed), builds the diagram with createElementNS from the shapes, accepting only numbers, the seven ink names mapped to CSS variables, dash patterns of digits and path data of M, H, V, L, Z and numbers, and places every string as textContent; The walk-through (stepWalk, drawWalk) keeps the walk's events in the view, calls WALK_TOOL (session_next) with them after each click, and builds every button and line as text nodes; MCPTests writes each view's script under .cache/tests and runs node --check on it, then runs scripts/session_view_smoke.js on the session view with the lending example's real session_check, session_simulate, session_conform, session_diagram, session_skeleton and session_next results: the script loads the view into a vm context with a stub DOM, canvas and host, completes the handshake, renders each result, walks through a choice (the deciding role shown choosing and the others waiting, undo, close) and toggles the animation's detail, and exits non-zero on any exception, rejected promise or missing control. session_simulate's events are drawn on a canvas with the prior, cause and answers of a selected event; the canvas starts simple (rows of 42 pixels, the newest LABELLED = 4 arrows labelled with their label and an error status, older ones at 35% opacity, prior links only for the selected event and its history) and More detail restores session tags, routes, statuses and every prior link at rows of 30 pixels. withSessionView attaches _meta.ui.resourceUri to the three tools; resources/read returns the compiled HTML with the logic view's empty CSP. The editor is a textarea filled once from the echoed lean text (later results redraw only the results container); input schedules a check after EDIT_PAUSE_MS = 700; run() allows only EDIT_TOOLS = [session_check, session_simulate], refuses empty text and text over MAX_EDIT_BYTES = 65536, keeps one call in flight and queues the latest edit, sends tools/call through the host with a 30-second timeout, and on -32601 or a timeout stops calling and says the host does not allow it; each animation has a generation number, so a replaced stream stops drawing."
      ["scripts/session_view_smoke.js: a whole-protocol result folds each role's typestate into its own panel, one under another, its header naming the role and its line count, and a panel of more than 15 lines starts folded and opens on click; the views bar shows the group tabs Structure, Roles, Behaviour, Properties and Code with only the shown group's views; a result's view lights its group; a group never looked at opens nothing; returning to Behaviour opens the walk-through it last showed again; every view the test drives is reached through its group tab", "LeanFM/MCPTests.lean: the session view is declared on exactly the three session tools; resources/read returns the compiled view with the MCP Apps MIME type and empty CSP domains; the view contains no network access, no innerHTML or other HTML insertion, no eval and no paths; it speaks the handshake and bounds the drawing (MAX_SHAPES = 4000, MAX_EVENTS = 600); the editor calls tools/call only for EDIT_TOOLS and bounds what it sends", "LeanFM/SessionTests.lean: every existing diagram test passes through the shape model"]
